From c987e9ff2b1e7688e17713955e018e63700643cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:49:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Admin booking requests: today by default, working filters,
 answer on a salon's behalf

The admin panel's Booking requests tab opened on "Today" and listed every
request the platform had ever taken: the list endpoint ignored the range
unless an explicit from/to came with it, and its default was all time. Two
controllers carried their own copy of the IST maths, and the service applied
the result by slicing ten characters off an ISO string and calling it UTC
midnight - a 5h30m shift that hid early-morning requests from "today".

- utils/istRange.js is now the single place a range becomes a pair of instants
  (TODAY by default, IST midnight to midnight, explicit bounds respected).
- The status filter and the search box were flattened into one OR, so either
  of them stopped filtering. They are separate AND groups now.
- The list returns per-status counts for the selected window, derived in SQL
  so auto-cancelled means the same thing to the chip as to the row.
- Ordering is stable (created_at DESC, id DESC) and the applied filters are
  echoed back, so the panel can print the window it is actually showing.
  Indexes added for the default view.

An admin may now answer a request on a salon's behalf. The old read-only rule
existed because a second accept path would create two bookings for one
request; that is answered here by not having a second path. Both
/owner-action and the new /admin/action call applyRequestAction, which locks
the row FOR UPDATE, refuses an already-answered or expired request, checks the
booking pointer before creating one, and records acted_by_role /
acted_by_admin_id / acted_at / on_behalf_of_salon. The salon is notified
either way.
